    "introduction": "Lily Du is a comedic performer and writer based in LA. She is a former cast member at CollegeHumor and currently hosts the boozy story-telling show Dirty Laundry on the Dropout streaming platform.She studied improv and sketch at the Upright Citizens Brigade Theater, where she performed on Harold Night and around the country with their Touring Company.Lily recurs on “New Amsterdam” (NBC) and “FBI” (CBS) and has appeared on \"The President Show,\" \"Broad City,\" & SyFy's \"Happy!\" opposite Chris Meloni. She has also hosted and been featured in videos on MTV’s Decoded, Funny Or Die and Comedy Central.Lily was a staff writer on “The Me And You Show” for Snapchat and wrote a short-form series about girls in STEM for Amy Poehler's Smart Girls. She has written joke punch-ups on the Paw Patrol movie and for Megan Thee Stallion. She has a pilot about toxic girl-boss feminism and another about Asian test-prep tutors. If you read them you’d love them.Lily grew up in Rockville, MD, and is a Smith College alum.",
